.archon/logs/iter-001/plan.jsonl:19:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- content.tex ---'; sed -n '1,260p' blueprint/src/content.tex; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- chapters ---'; rg --files blueprint/src/chapters | sort; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- coverage ---'; rg -n '\"'^% archon:covers|'\"\\\\\\\\lean\\\\{' blueprint/src/chapters | head -n 500\"","aggregated_output":"--- content.tex ---\n% In this file you should put the actual content of the blueprint.\n% It will be used both by the web and the print version.\n% It should *not* include the \\begin{document}\n%\n% If you want to split the blueprint content into several files then\n% the current file can be a simple sequence of \\input. Otherwise It\n% can start with a \\section or \\chapter for instance.\n\n\\part{Brownian motion}\n\n\\textbf{Overview}\n\nThis part of the blueprint is a guide to the formalization of a standard Brownian motion in Lean using Mathlib. There are two main parts to this formalization:\n\\begin{itemize}\n  \\item a development of the theory of Gaussian distributions, the construction of a projective family of Gaussian distributions and its projective limit by the Kolmogorov extension theorem,\n  \\item a proof of a Kolmogorov-Chentsov continuity theorem, following \\cite{kratschmer2023kolmogorov}.\n\\end{itemize}\n\nPutting the two sides together, we then build a stochastic process that fits the definition of a Brownian motion on the real line.\n\n\\textbf{Status} The formalization is complete.\n\n\\textbf{Blueprint authors} Rémy Degenne, Peter Pfaffelhuber.\n\n\\textbf{Formalization authors} Rémy Degenne, Markus Himmel, David Ledvinka, Etienne Marion, Peter Pfaffelhuber.\n\nWith additional contributions from Jonas Bayer, Lorenzo Loccioli, Pietro Monticone, Alessio Rondelli and Jérémy Scanvic.\n\n\\input{chapters/characteristic_function.tex}\n\\input{chapters/process.tex}\n\\input{chapters/gaussian.tex}\n\\input{chapters/projective_family.tex}\n\\input{chapters/kolmogorov_chentsov.tex}\n\\input{chapters/brownian.tex}\n\n\\putbib\n\n\\part{Stochastic integral}\n\n\\textbf{Overview}\n\nWe describe the construction of a stochastic integral.\n\n\\textbf{Status} The formalization is ongoing.\n\n\\textbf{Blueprint authors} Rémy Degenne, Lorenzo Luccioli, Etienne Marion, Alessio Rondelli, Kexing Ying. Anyone is welcome to contribute!\n\n\\textbf{Formalization authors} Anyone is welcome to contribute!\n\n\\input{chapters/filtration_martingale.tex}\n\\input{chapters/debut.tex}\n\\input{chapters/local_martingales.tex}\n\\input{chapters/elementary.tex}\n\\input{chapters/cadlag.tex}\n\\input{chapters/doob_meyer.tex}\n\\input{chapters/stochastic_integral.tex}\n\n\\putbib\n--- chapters ---\nblueprint/src/chapters/brownian.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/cadlag.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/characteristic_function.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/debut.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/doob_meyer.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/elementary.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/gaussian.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/kolmogorov_chentsov.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/process.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/projective_family.tex\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex\n--- coverage ---\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:14:  \\lean{StieltjesFunction.measure}\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:37:  \\lean{eVariationOn}\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:46:  \\lean{BoundedVariationOn}\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:54:  \\lean{LocallyBoundedVariationOn}\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:62:  %\\lean{BoundedVariationOn.vectorMeasure}\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:127:  \\lean{ProbabilityTheory.IsSquareIntegrable}\nblueprint/src/chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:136:  \\lean{ProbabilityTheory.IsSquareIntegrable.add, ProbabilityTheory.IsSquareIntegra